<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "A P2P session can run in a browser tab of its own, with the whole window to itself. In the starting room, choose Open in a tab. It is the same session either way — the chat keeps its P2P window for when you would rather not leave the page."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "Sharing the address")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Share mints a link you can paste anywhere. The link names the session and never grants access to it: only the two people already in it can enter, and anyone else who follows it gets a card explaining that."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_window_restore}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "One window at a time")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "A session can only be live in one of your windows. Opening it somewhere else moves it there, and the window that lost it says so and offers Bring it back here. Closing the tab is not ending the session: the stop button and the window's X ask first, and only they are final."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_p2p", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-p2p-in-chat">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "P2P Sessions in Chat")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-p2p-starting-room">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "P2P Starting Room")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
